            "author_association": "MEMBER",
            "body": "> I believe this happens when you jump back in your history and have a file open in nvim that did not exist back then.\n\nThen absence of `vim.b.minidiff_summary` is somewhat expected.\n\n> I could just now reproduce this with a simple `rm`:\n\n~~I also could kind of reproduce, but not exactly reliably. I'll take a look at what is the best approach here is.~~ It was a side effect of something else I am testing.\n\nI can not reproduce this, i.e. after step 4. there is no `MiniDiffUpdated` event triggered. Although the Git source is still attached, the reference text is `nil` and `vim.b.minidiff_summary` is  just `{ source_name = 'git' }`.",
