            "author_association": "NONE",
            "body": "Having the same difficulty as you to reproduce.\n\nI assume it happens if some specific pre-condition is met and the buffer/repo is in a weird state. The issue is fairly consistent and I've had it occasionally for some weeks now, I just could not pay much attention, because I was always at work and though \"I'll fix/report later\".\n\nJust for context I've observed 2 variations of this issue:\n1. The one from my original post with `summary.add`, `summary.change` and `summary.delete`   being `nil`\n2. The one below with `summary = nil`\n\n```\nError in User Autocommands for \"MiniDiffUpdated\":\nLua callback: /home/matt/.config/nvim-repro/init.lua:23: attempt to index local 'summary' (a nil value)\nstack traceback:\n        /home/matt/.config/nvim-repro/init.lua:23: in function </home/matt/.config/nvim-repro/init.lua:20>\n        [C]: in function 'nvim_exec_autocmds'\n        ...vim-repro/site/pack/core/opt/mini.nvim/lua/mini/diff.lua:1315: in function ''\n        vim/_editor.lua: in function <vim/_editor.lua:0>\nPress ENTER or type command to continue\n```\n\n### Minimal Example\n\nThis works for both issues.  (I just cannot figure out how to trigger No.1 in a reliable way yet.)\n\n```lua\n-- ~/.config/nvim-repro/init.lua\nvim.pack.add({\n\t{ src = \"https://github.com/nvim-mini/mini.nvim\" },\n})\n\nrequire(\"mini.diff\").setup()\nrequire(\"mini.git\").setup()\n\nvim.api.nvim_create_autocmd(\"User\", {\n\tpattern = \"MiniGitUpdated\",\n\tcallback = function(data)\n\t\tlocal summary = vim.b.minigit_summary\n\t\tlocal head = summary.head_name or \"\"\n\t\thead = head == \"HEAD\" and summary.head:sub(1, 8) or head\n\t\tvim.b[data.buf].minigit_summary_string = head\n\tend\n})\n\nvim.api.nvim_create_autocmd(\"User\", {\n\tpattern = \"MiniDiffUpdated\",\n\tcallback = function(data)\n\t\tlocal summary = vim.b[data.buf].minidiff_summary\n\t\tlocal t = {}\n\t\tif summary.add > 0 then table.insert(t, \" +\" .. summary.add) end\n\t\tif summary.change > 0 then table.insert(t, \" ~\" .. summary.change) end\n\t\tif summary.delete > 0 then table.insert(t, \" -\" .. summary.delete) end\n\t\tvim.b[data.buf].minidiff_summary_string = table.concat(t)\n\tend\n})\n\nlocal function git()\n\tlocal branch, status = vim.b.minigit_summary_string, vim.b.minidiff_summary_string\n\treturn branch and status and \"[ \" .. branch .. status .. \"]\" or \"\"\nend\n\nUser = {}\nfunction User.statusline()\n\treturn table.concat({ \"%<%f %h%w%m%r\", git(), \"%=\", \"%-14.(%l,%c%V%) %P\" })\nend\n\nvim.opt.statusline = \"%!v:lua.User.statusline()\"\n\n```\n\n### Repro\n\nHere repro for issue 2. (I'll keep trying for the first one and update)\n\n```\n# Pane 1 (cli):\nmkdir -p ~/.config/nvim-repro\ncp ~/Downloads/init.lua ~/.config/nvim-repro\ncd ~/.config/nvim-repro\ngit init\ngit add .\ngit commit -m 'initial commit'\n\n# Pane 2 (nvim):\ncd ~/.config/nvim-repro\nNVIM_APPNAME=nvim-repro nvim init.lua\n:e foo.txt\n:w\n\n# Pane 1 (cli):\ngit add .\n\n=> error message appears in nvim\n```\n\n### Additional Info\nOS: Arch Linux\nGit version: 2.51.1\nNVIM v0.12.0-dev-1482+gaf0f7b59b1\n\n",
