            "author_association": "MEMBER",
            "body": "Thanks, I can reproduce 2. The reason was the one that I suspected at first: event is triggered *for* the different buffer (for 'init.lua' in the repro) while *other* buffer is active which gives `data.buf` point at not the correct buffer identifier.\n\nIn similar situation 'mini.git' [does account for that](https://github.com/nvim-mini/mini.nvim/blob/64a23d04cce6d600f18d5d1610d319f6efa08958/lua/mini/git.lua#L1478-L1479). I probably forgot to adjust 'mini.diff'. I'll add it later.\n\n---\n\n> 1. The one from my original post with `summary.add`, `summary.change` and `summary.delete`   being `nil`\n\nThis is possible if source is attached but `ref_text` is not set. It can be better documented, though. I'll also take a look.",
